},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":634,"col":40},"end":{"line":634,"col":41}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":9618,"kind":{"StorageDead":3},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":635,"col":5},"end":{"line":635,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":9619,"kind":{"StorageDead":5},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":635,"col":5},"end":{"line":635,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":9620,"kind":{"StorageDead":2},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":635,"col":5},"end":{"line":635,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":9621,"kind":{"StorageDead":1},"comments_before":[]},{"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":635,"col":5},"end":{"line":635,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"id":9622,"kind":"Return","comments_before":[]}]},"comments":[]}}},{"def_id":118,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["iter",0]},{"Ident":["traits",0]},{"Ident":["iterator",0]},{"Ident":["Iterator",0]},{"Ident":["intersperse",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":693,"col":4},"end":{"line":696,"col":26}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Creates a new iterator which places a copy of `separator` between items"},{"DocComment":" of the original iterator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Specifically on fused iterators, it is guaranteed that the new iterator"},{"DocComment":" places a copy of `separator` between *adjacent* `Some(_)` items. For non-fused iterators,"},{"DocComment":" it is guaranteed that [`intersperse`] will create a new iterator that places a copy"},{"DocComment":" of `separator` between `Some(_)` items, particularly just right before the subsequent"},{"DocComment":" `Some(_)` item."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For example, consider the following non-fused iterator:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```text"},{"DocComment":" Some(1) -> Some(2) -> None -> Some(3) -> Some(4) -> ..."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If this non-fused iterator were to be interspersed with `0`,"},{"DocComment":" then the interspersed iterator will produce:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```text"},{"DocComment":" Some(1) -> Some(0) -> Some(2) -> None -> Some(0) -> Some(3) -> Some(0) ->"},{"DocComment":" Some(4) -> ..."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In case `separator` does not implement [`Clone`] or needs to be"},{"DocComment":" computed every time, use [`intersperse_with`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #![feature(iter_intersperse)]"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut a = [0, 1, 2].into_iter().intersperse(100);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(0));   // The first element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(100)); // The separator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(1));   // The next element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(100)); // The separator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(2));   // The last element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), None);       // The iterator is finished."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `intersperse` can be very useful to join an iterator's items using a common element:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #![feature(iter_intersperse)]"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let words = [\"Hello\", \"World\", \"!\"];"},{"DocComment":" let hello: String = words.into_iter().intersperse(\" \").collect();"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(hello, \"Hello World !\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`Clone`]: crate::clone::Clone"},{"DocComment":" [`intersperse`]: Iterator::intersperse"},{"DocComment":" [`intersperse_with`]: Iterator::intersperse_with"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local"