gth_prefix` before calling this."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Note to Implementers"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" There are at least two reasonable default ways to implement this."},{"DocComment":" Which one will be the default is not yet decided, so for now"},{"DocComment":" you probably want to override it specifically."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## The general answer"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" It's always correct to implement this with a length prefix:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # #![feature(hasher_prefixfree_extras)]"},{"DocComment":" # struct Foo;"},{"DocComment":" # impl std::hash::Hasher for Foo {"},{"DocComment":" # fn finish(&self) -> u64 { unimplemented!() }"},{"DocComment":" # fn write(&mut self, _bytes: &[u8]) { unimplemented!() }"},{"DocComment":" fn write_str(&mut self, s: &str) {"},{"DocComment":"     self.write_length_prefix(s.len());"},{"DocComment":"     self.write(s.as_bytes());"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" # }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" And, if your `Hasher` works in `usize` chunks, this is likely a very"},{"DocComment":" efficient way to do it, as anything more complicated may well end up"},{"DocComment":" slower than just running the round with the length."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ## If your `Hasher` works byte-wise"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" One nice thing about `str` being UTF-8 is that the `b'\\xFF'` byte"},{"DocComment":" never happens.  That means that you can append that to the byte stream"},{"DocComment":" being hashed and maintain prefix-freedom:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # #![feature(hasher_prefixfree_extras)]"},{"DocComment":" # struct Foo;"},{"DocComment":" # impl std::hash::Hasher for Foo {"},{"DocComment":" # fn finish(&self) -> u64 { unimplemented!() }"},{"DocComment":" # fn write(&mut self, _bytes: &[u8]) { unimplemented!() }"},{"DocComment":" fn write_str(&mut self, s: &str) {"},{"DocComment":"     self.write(s.as_bytes());"},{"DocComment":"     self.write_u8(0xff);"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" # }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This does require that your implementation not add extra padding, and"},{"DocComment":" thus generally requires that you maintain a buffer, running a round"},{"DocComment":" only once that buffer is full (or `finish` is called)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" That's because if `write` pads data out to a fixed chunk size, it's"},{"DocComment":" likely that it does it in such a way that `\"a\"` and `\"a\\x00\"` would"},{"DocComment":" end up hashing the same sequence of things, introducing conflicts."}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"},{"index":1,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":1,"beg":{"line":1,"col":0},"end":{"line":1,"col":0}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":58,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":49597}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":49653},{"HashConsedValue":[52699,{"Ref":[{"Var":{"Free":1}},{"Deduplicated":9196},"Shared"]}]}],"output":{"Deduplicated":1764}},"src":{"TraitDecl":{"trait_ref":{"id":58,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":49597}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}},"item_id":{"Method":15}}},"is_global_initializer":null,"body":{"Structured":{"span":{"data":{"file_id":114,"beg":{"line":550,"col":4},"end":{"line":553,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"bound_body_regions":10,"locals":{"arg_count":2,"locals":[{"index":0,"name":null,"span":{"data":{"f