",0]},{"Ident":["partial_cmp",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":33,"beg":{"line":3808,"col":4},"end":{"line":3812,"col":20}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" [Lexicographically](Ord#lexicographical-comparison) compares the [`PartialOrd`] elements of"},{"DocComment":" this [`Iterator`] with those of another. The comparison works like short-circuit"},{"DocComment":" evaluation, returning a result without comparing the remaining elements."},{"DocComment":" As soon as an order can be determined, the evaluation stops and a result is returned."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::cmp::Ordering;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([1.].iter().partial_cmp([1.].iter()), Some(Ordering::Equal));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([1.].iter().partial_cmp([1., 2.].iter()), Some(Ordering::Less));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([1., 2.].iter().partial_cmp([1.].iter()), Some(Ordering::Greater));"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For floating-point numbers, NaN does not have a total order and will result"},{"DocComment":" in `None` when compared:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([f64::NAN].iter().partial_cmp([1.].iter()), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The results are determined by the order of evaluation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::cmp::Ordering;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([1.0, f64::NAN].iter().partial_cmp([2.0, f64::NAN].iter()), Some(Ordering::Less));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([2.0, f64::NAN].iter().partial_cmp([1.0, f64::NAN].iter()), Some(Ordering::Greater));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!([f64::NAN, 1.0].iter().partial_cmp([f64::NAN, 2.0].iter()), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":n